        "subject": "LU-20076 lnet: abort socket connects when LNet stops",
        "message": "LU-20076 lnet: abort socket connects when LNet stops\n\nA socket LND connect to an address that does not answer lasts\nas long as the kernel's SYN retries, about 127 seconds, and\nLNet shutdown waits for it twice. The discovery thread waits\nfor its ping message, which the LND holds until the connect\nfails, and ksocknal_shutdown() waits for the peer that the\nconnd thread holds. conf-sanity tests that leave peers with\nunreachable NIDs, such as 31 and 153a or 32a and 32d with the\nNIDs of the upgrade images, took 78 to 129 seconds to unload\nthe modules.\n\nKeep the sockets being connected on a list, and shut them\ndown when LNet begins to stop. A connect that has not started\nto wait finds a zero send timeout and returns at once, and no\nnew connect starts while LNet stops. An aborted connect\nreturns -ESHUTDOWN, which is not reported on the console.\n\nOn a three node ldiskfs cluster with the other open LU-20076\nchanges, conf-sanity 31, 32a to 32d, 73c, 78, 153a, 153c and\n158 took 1040 and 956 s rather than 1779 and 1642 s. Module\nunloads in 31, 32a, 32d, 153a, 153c and 158 took 627 s in all\nin each run before, and none took more than 2 s after.\n\nTest-Parameters: testlist=conf-sanity env=ONLY=\"31 32a 32d 73c 153a 158\"\nTest-Parameters: testlist=sanity-lnet\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5\nSigned-off-by: Patrick Farrell <patrick@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: I577fd81f3e4b98a650c957c515ee6b1bbfba997d\n"
      },
